Venetium 0057 - honour the page's own preconnect / dns-prefetch hints while "Preload pages" stays off.
From the performance research (C:\handoff\PERF-RESEARCH.md, item N1), his "fix all".
0005 makes "Preload pages" off the default (NetworkPredictionOptions::kDisabled). Besides stopping predictive
preconnects, that made the PreconnectManager refuse every request, including the hints a page asks for itself:
<link rel=preconnect>, <link rel=dns-prefetch> and Link: headers reach chrome/browser/predictors/
network_hints_handler_impl.cc and were silently dropped (preconnect_manager_impl.cc returns early on every entry point).
Those hints only reach origins the page is about to load from anyway, so with preloading off the handler now serves
them straight from the frame's network context (PreconnectSockets / a speculative, idle-priority ResolveHost), the way
Android WebView and content_shell do (components/network_hints/browser/simple_network_hints_handler_impl.cc), with the
pending NetworkAnonymizationKey and the frame's network restrictions. Predictive preconnects (omnibox, search engine,
history, hover) still go through the PreconnectManager and stay off; off-the-record profiles still get no hints;
with "Preload pages" turned on everything goes the stock way. web.dev puts a preconnect to a critical third-party
origin at 100-500 ms saved.

